Sure! I'll revise the `paraphrase` function to streamline the logic. Here's the updated code:

```javascript
// src/paraphrase.js
function paraphrase(text) {
    const processedText = text
        .replace(/\b(?:very|really|extremely)\b/g, 'some')
        .replace(/\b(?:quick|fast)\b/g, 'speedy')
        .replace(/\b(?:happy|joyful)\b/g, 'cheerful');
    return processedText;
}

module.exports = paraphrase;
```

I'll also update the tests in `paraphrase.test.js` to ensure we cover these changes:

```javascript
// test/paraphrase.test.js
const paraphrase = require('../src/paraphrase');

test('paraphrases text correctly', () => {
    expect(paraphrase('She is very happy.')).toBe('She is some cheerful.');
    expect(paraphrase('He runs fast.')).toBe('He runs speedy.');
});
```

